SECURITY

- Never commit .env. It holds GNANI_API_KEY, GROQ_API_KEY, R2 keys, and
  BETTER_AUTH_SECRET. The repo's .env.example has blanks only.
- ENABLE_DEV_AUTH must never be true in production. It bypasses auth.
- Put TLS at a reverse proxy (Caddy/nginx/Cloudflare). Do not expose the
  API directly to the internet without it.
- Restrict SSH ingress to your own IP and keep the R2 bucket private;
  audio links are presigned and expire.

Report a vulnerability by opening a private issue on the GitHub repo.
